hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10066","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr told me, on the authority of Saeed, that the father of the men was Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman He narrated to him, on the authority of his mother Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a man on a convoy, and he used to read to his companions in Their prayer was concluded with: Say, He is God, One. When they returned, they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Ask him for what he did.” “That?” They asked him, and he said: It is an attribute of the Most Gracious, and I like to recite it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tell him.” “God loves him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10067","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he said: “I was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting: ‘Say, O you disbelievers’ until he concluded it and said: He has been exonerated.” This is polytheism. Then we walked and he heard another person reciting: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One.’” So he said: “As for this man, he has been forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10068","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Saeed, that Abu al-Musaffa told him that Ibn Abi Laila Al-Ansari told him, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey while we were walking, and a man from My people, say, O you disbelievers. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for your companion, he has been freed from polytheism.” So I went to see who So I gave him good tidings, then another man recited: Say, He is God, One. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for your companion, his has been forgiven.”"
"10069","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Shababah told us, he said: He is Ibn Muslim Al-Khurasani, Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not sleep every night until he had recited the revelation of the prostration, and blessed be He in whose hand is the dominion.” Laith bin Abi Sulaym followed him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10070","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hassan ibn Salih, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, does not sleep every night until he recites: Al-M {1} Revealing the prostration, and blessed be He in whose hand is the dominion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10071","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Ayan, told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not sleep until he had recited Al-Ma’am Revelation, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"10072","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: I asked Abu Al-Zubayr: Did you hear Jabir mention, “Indeed the Prophet By God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would not sleep until he recited the verse “The Revelation of God and Blessed be He.” He said: Jabir did not narrate to me, but Safwan or Ibn Safwan narrated to me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10073","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I said to Abu Usama: I am telling you about Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abbas al-Jashmi, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, there is a surah in the Qur’an of thirty verses that intercedes for its companion until he is forgiven: Blessed is He who In His hand is the kingdom.” Abu Usama acknowledged it and said: Yes."
"10074","Ubayd Allah ibn Abdul Karim told us, and he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah Abu Thabit al-Madani told us, he said: Ibn Abi Hazim told us, On the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Arfaja bin Abdul Wahid, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, He said: “Whoever recites: Blessed is He in whose hand is the kingdom, every night, God will protect him from the torment of the grave.” And we were in the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We call it Al-Mani’ah, and it is in the Book of God a surah. Whoever recites it every night will increase in number and become happy. Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10075","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar informed us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Marwan Abu Lubabah, that Aisha said: “The Messenger of God was He, may God bless him and grant him peace, would fast until we said: He does not want to fast, and he would break his fast until we say: What he wants to fast, and he would recite every night: Israel, and the tribes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10076","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Baqiya bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Bilal, on the authority of Al-Irbad Ibn Sariyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Rosary before he lay down, and he would say: “Indeed “In it is one verse better than a thousand verses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10077","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, On the authority of Ibn Abi Bilal, on the authority of Al-Irbad ibn Sariyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the rosary before he lay down, and he said: “ Indeed, therein is a sign better than a thousand signs.” Muawiyah bin Saleh disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10078","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: I heard Muawiyah speaking, on the authority of Buhair ibn Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not sleep until he had recited the Rosaries, and he would say: “Indeed, in them is a sign like a thousand verses.” Muawiyah said: Some people of knowledge used to make the Rosaries six: Surat Al-Hadid, Al-Hashr, Al-Hawwariyyin, and Surat Al-Jumu’ah. , and the absence of ignorance, and glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found blackness on the edge of the book at the bottom of this hadith, so for that reason I did not write: He narrated to us."
"10079","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Sa`id told us, he said: Ayyash bin Abbas told us, on the authority of Issa bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Read to me, O Messenger of God. He said: Recite three of the literal meanings. “The man said: Have my years grown, my heart hardened, and my tongue thickened?” He said: “Recite three of the Dhawat (Ham),” he said like his first saying. He said: “Recite three of the Rosaries,” and he said like his first saying. So he said: “Recite three of the Rosaries.” He said the same as his first statement, he said: “But recite to me a comprehensive Surah.” So he recited it: “When I am shaken.” The earth was shaken until it was finished. The man said: By the One who has sent you with the truth, I will never do more than that. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Ruwaijal succeeded, the Ruwaijal succeeded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10080","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf and Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ told me, they said: Haitham bin Humaid told us, he said: Zaid bin Waqid told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites one hundred verses in one night, Qunut of the night will be recorded for him.”"
"10081","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah - whoever recites them in the night That's enough for him"
"10082","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, He said: The hadith was mentioned to me on the authority of Abu Masoud, so I met him while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, so I asked him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever recites the last two verses of Surat Al-Baqarah in one night, it is sufficient for him.”"
"10083","Kathir ibn Khalid told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jaafar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the last two verses of Al-Baqarah in the night \It's enough for him.\"" Abu Abdul Rahman said: I met Abu Masoud and he told me about him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10084","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two verses are from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah. Whoever recites them in one night is sufficient for him.”"
"10085","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with us and was with him.” Gabriel, when he heard the opposite above it, so Gabriel raised his gaze to the sky, and said: This is a door that has been opened from the sky that had never been opened, he said: So he descended. An angel came from it, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Give good tidings of two lights that you have been given that were not given to a prophet before you: The Opening of the Book And the endings of Surat Al-Baqarah, you will not recite a letter of them unless you give it away.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10086","Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Karim told us, he said: Ali bin Abdul Majeed told us, he said: Sulayman bin Al Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on his way, and he came down and a man came down beside him, and he turned to him and said: “Shall I not tell you?” With the best of the Qur’an? He said: So he recited to him: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10087","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, saying: Abu Muammar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah told me, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “They do not say One of you said: “Indeed, I forgot the verse of Kit and Kit, so it is not he who forgot, but he forgot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10088","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Let none of you say: I forgot the verse of such-and-such, but rather he forgot.”"
"10089","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How miserable is it for one of you to say: I forgot one verse and another, but rather he forgot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10090","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym and Muawiyah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How evil is it for one of them to say: I forgot a verse like this and another, but rather he forgot.”"
"10091","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: “How wretched is the For one of them to say: I forgot the verse of Kit and Kit, but rather he forgot.”"
"10092","Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, On the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka`b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It is recited in the Witr prayer with: Praise the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, “O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, the One.’” Then, when he said the salutation, he said: “Glory be to the King.” “The Holy One” three times. Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib disagreed with him and did not mention Ubayy (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10093","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq, who is Ibn Mansour, told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of his Witr prayer: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times, extending the The last of them. Zubaid agreed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10094","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad told us, my father told us, he said: Jarir told us, he said: I heard Zubaid talking, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord Most High and say, O The disbelievers and say, “He is God, the One.” And when he said the salutation, he said: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times, extending his voice the third time and raising it. He was sent by Malik bin Mughal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10095","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abza, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High” and say, “O you disbelievers,” and say, “He is God, One.” And when he finishes, he says: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times, then he extends his voice at the end."
"10096","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High” and say, “O you disbelievers,” and say, “He is God, One.” And when he finished, he said: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10097","Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray Witr with three rak’ahs, reciting in the first with: “Glorify the name of God.” Your Lord is the Most High, and in the second verse: Say, O you disbelievers, and in the third verse: Say, He is God, the One. And when he finished, he said: “Glory be to the King.” “The Holy One,” and he says Qunoot before bowing. When he finishes, he says: “Glory be to the King, the Holy Ones” three times, prolonging the last of them."
"10098","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, O O disbelievers, say, “He is God, the One.” And he says after the salutation: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times, raising his voice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10099","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: “Glorify the name of your Lord.” The highest, and say, “O you disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, One.’” When he wanted to leave, he said: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times. He raises his voice with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10100","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, and Zubaid, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Most High Lord and say, O The disbelievers, and say: He is God, the One. And when he said the salutation: “Glory be to the King, the Holy,” three times, he would raise his voice a third time."
"10101","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Salamah and Zubaid told me, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the Witr prayer: “Glorify the name of your Lord” The highest, and say, “O you disbelievers,” and say, “He is God, the One.” Then he says when he greets: “Glory be to the Holy King, Glory be to the Holy King.” He raises his voice for a third time. Mansour agreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Salamah 63, on the authority of Saeed, and he did not mention a single bit. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10102","Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of His father, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite the verse: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is God, One.’” And He was When he said the salaam and finished, he said: “Glory be to the King” three times, lengthening the third time. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10103","Yahya bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Khalid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It is recited in the Witr prayer with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in the second rak’ah with: Say, O you disbelievers, and in the third with: Say, He is God. And he does not say the salutation except at the last of them, and he says after the salutation: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times. Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad and Muhammad ibn Bishr opposed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10104","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High and say” O you disbelievers, say, “He is God, the One.” When he finished his Witr prayer, he said: “Glory be to the Holy King.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10105","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the verse: Praise the name of your Most High Lord and say, O The unbelievers and say, “He is God, the One.” Then when he greets, he says three times: “Glory be to the King, the Holy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10106","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Ezra talking, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord Most High and say, O O disbelievers, say: He is God, the One. Then, when he finishes, he says: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10107","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Zurara speaking On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord Most High and say, O The disbelievers and say, “He is God, the One.” Then when he greets, he says: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times and extends it the third time."
"10108","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Extinguish the lamp, and mention the name of God, and cover the vessels, even if you display them with a stick, and mention the name of God.”"
"10109","Ahmad bin Uthman told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ata’ told me that he heard Jabir, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Close your doors, and mention the name of God, for Satan does not open what is closed, and rest in peace.” Your closeness, and mention the name of God, and cover your utensils, and mention the name of God, even if you display something on them, and extinguish the lamps.” Ibn Jurayj said: Amr ibn Dinar told me that he heard Jabir tell something similar to what Ataa told me, except that he did not say: “Mention the name of God.” \""
10110"""
"10110","'Amr ibn Mansur informed me, saying: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abdul-Malik, from al-Rabi'i, from Hudhayfah, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to sleep, he would say: ""In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live."""
"10111","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Malik Bin Umair, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, He said: “In your name, O God, I live and die.”"
"10112","Muhammad ibn Adam told us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he said: “O God, in your name I live and die.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10113","Muhammad ibn Idris told me, he said: Adam told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Kharsha ibn al-Harr, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, he would say: “In your name I die and I live.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10114","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Suwayd informed us, he said: Ghandar informed us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar informed us He said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa speaking, on the authority of Al-Baraa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say that if he wanted to He sleeps: “In your name I live, and in your name I die.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10115","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he placed his right hand under his right cheek and said: “Save me from your punishment on the day you resurrect your servants.”"
"10116","Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Ashja’i told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God was when He went to bed and put his right hand under his right cheek, then said: “O God, protect me from your torment on the day You resurrect your servants.”"
"10117","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, and another man, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to sleep, he would place his right hand on his pillow and say: “Oh God, protect us from your torment.” The day you gather your servants.” And the other said: “the day you raise your servants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10118","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would place his right hand under his cheek and say: “O God, protect me from your punishment on the day you are resurrected.” \Your servants\"""""
"10119","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would place his right hand under his cheek and say: “O God, protect me from your torment on the Day of You gather your servants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10120","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would say: “Oh God, protect me from your torment on the day you are resurrected.” \Your servants\"""""
"10121","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibrahim, who is the son of Yusuf, told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said Abu Burdah told me on the authority of Al-Baraa. He heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lean on his right hand when he slept and put it under the His cheek, and he says: “Oh God, protect me from your punishment on the day you resurrect your servants.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It is similar to it being: on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq."
"10122","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Yazid informed us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of Uthman bin Amr, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abdul Rahman Al Ansari, on the authority of Al Rabi’ bin Al Bara’ bin Azib, said: Al Bara’ bin Azib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever speaks these words when he takes his side from his bed after the evening prayer and then dies during that night will enter Paradise: Oh God. I have surrendered my religion to you, and I have turned my face to you, and I have entrusted my affairs to you, and I have turned my back to you. There is no refuge from you except in you. I have believed. By Your Messenger whom You have sent, and by Your Book which You have sent down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10123","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Muhammad, who is Ibn Amr, speaking, He said: Rabi’, who is Ibn Lot bin Al-Baraa, narrated to me on the authority of his uncle Al-Baraa bin Azib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He took his bed, placed his right palm under his right forehead, and said: “My Lord, save me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10124","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, On the authority of Sawa Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Hafsa bint Omar, may God be pleased with them, she said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would seek refuge in On his bed, he placed his right hand under his cheek and said: “My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10125","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Ma’bad Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Sawa, on the authority of Hafsa bint Omar, that when the Messenger wanted to lie down, he would place his right hand under his right cheek, And he said: “Oh God, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10126","Ali bin Harb told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Yazid, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sawa Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would place his right palm under his right cheek.”"
"10127","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: “It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would place his right palm under his right cheek.”"
"10128","Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us words to say when sleeping out of fear: “In the name of God, I seek refuge With the perfect words of God from His wrath, and from His punishment, and from the evil of His servants, and from the prodding of the devils, and that they come.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10129","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: Khalid bin Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah was a man who would panic in his sleep, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “When you lie down, say: In the name of God. I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, from His wrath and punishment, and from The evil of His servants, and from the promptings of the devils, and that they may be present.” So he said it and that went away from him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10130","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Al-Ahwas, meaning Ibn Jawab, told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, and Abi Maysarah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say when he lay down: “O God, I seek refuge in With your generous face, and with your perfect words, from the evil that you are taking by the corner of it, O God, you reveal the sin and the debt, O God, do not Your army will be defeated, your promise will not be broken, and your hard work will not benefit from you. Glory be to You and praise be to You.”"
"10131","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, that When he slept, he would say: “O God, I have surrendered myself to You, and I have turned my face to You, and I have entrusted my affairs to You, and I have turned my back to You, and I have believed.” By your revealed Book, and by your sent Prophet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10132","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, He said: “When you go to bed, say: In the name of God, in the path of God, and according to the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when you enter the dead in his grave\""
10133"""
"10133","Yunus ibn 'Abdul-A'la informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Hayyah narrated to me, from Abu 'Abdur-Rahman al-Hubuli, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that when he lay down to sleep, he would say: ""O Allah, in Your name, my Lord, I have placed my side (to sleep), so forgive me my sin."""
"10134","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub and Abu Dawud told us, saying: Othman bin Omar told us, saying: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he lies down One of you on his right side, let him say: O God, I have surrendered my religion to You, I have turned my face to You, I have turned my back to You, and I have entrusted “My command is to you. There is no escape from you except to you. If he dies that night, he will enter Paradise.” Abraham added in his speech: “And I believe in you and your messengers.”"
"10135","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to me, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Safar, He heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrating, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Aazib, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asleep, he would say: In your name I live and die.” And when he woke up, he would say: “Praise be to God who brought us back to life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.”"
"10136","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Uthman bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, that a man said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What should I say when I go to My bed? He said: “Say, O God, I have surrendered myself to You, and I have turned my face to You, and I have turned my back to You, out of desire and fear for You, there is neither refuge nor There is no escape from you except to you. I believe in your book which you sent down, and in your prophet whom you were sent. If you die, you will die following the fitrah. And if you become “Good night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10137","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib told us, he said: Ibrahim, who is the son of Al-Hajjaj, told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, and Habib bin Al-Shahid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a example: It was When he goes to bed, he says: “O God, I have surrendered myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and sought refuge in You.” My back, and I raised my desire to you, out of desire and awe of you, I believed in the Book you sent down and the Messenger you sent.” He added to it: “There is no refuge or refuge from you except to you. I believe in your book which you sent down, and in your messenger whom you sent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10138","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Al-Baraa, he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructing a man, when he went to bed, to say: “O God, I surrender myself to you. And I turned my face to You, and I entrusted my affairs to You, and I turned my back to You, out of desire and fear for You. There is no refuge or refuge from You except from You. To you, I believe in your prophet whom you sent, and in your book which you sent down, so if he dies, he dies according to the fitrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10139","Muhammad bin Ismail told us, he said: Ali bin Hafs told us, he said: Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you go to your bed, say: O God, I surrender myself to You and turn my face to You. And I entrusted my affairs to you, and I turned my back to you, out of desire and fear for you. There is no refuge or refuge from you except in you. I believed in your book which You were sent down, and by your Prophet whom You sent, so if you die during that night, you will die following the fitrah, and if you wake up in the morning, you will become good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10140","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us. And Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “O so-and-so, when you take your bed, say: O God, I surrender myself to you, and direct myself to you.” I turned my face to You, and I entrusted my affairs to You, and I turned my back to You, out of fear and desire for You. I believed in Your Book which You revealed, and in Your Prophet. What you were sent for, if something happens to you during your night, then you die, and you are on the right path, and if you wake up in the morning, you do well, and you have achieved good.” He said: Abu Ishaq used to add to it: “There is no refuge or refuge from you except to you,” and he said: I did not hear this from Al-Bara’, I heard them. They mention to him, “There is no refuge or refuge.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10141","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He went to his bed and said: “O God, I have surrendered myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and turned my back to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed, and in Your Messenger whom You sent.” Laith disagreed with them. Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Laith mentioning, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you go to bed,” and similar to it. Mu’tamar said: He told me Al-Hajjaj and others narrated it, on the authority of Abu Ishaq (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10142","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, and Abu Dawud told us, they said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Saad bin Ubaidah narrating, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded a man when he went to bed to He says: “O God, I have surrendered myself to You, and I have turned my face to You, and I have turned my back to You, and I have entrusted my affairs to You, out of desire and fear.” To You, there is no refuge or refuge from You except in You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed, and in Your Messenger whom You have sent. If he dies, he dies according to the fitrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10143","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you come Your bed, so perform your ablution for prayer, then let the last thing you say be: O God, I have surrendered my face to You, I have entrusted my affairs to You, and I have sought refuge. My back is to you, out of desire and fear for you, there is no refuge or refuge from you except in you. I believe in your book which you have sent down, and in your prophet whom you have sent. If you die, you die on fitrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10144","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Mansour speaking, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, he said: He told us Al-Baraa bin Azib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “When you go to bed, perform your ablution for prayer, then lie down.” On your right side, say: O God, I have surrendered my face to You, and I have entrusted my affairs to You, out of fear and desire for You, there is no refuge or refuge except from You. To you, I believe in your book which you sent down, and in your prophet whom you sent, so if you die, you will die on the right path, and make them the last thing you say,” Al-Baraa said, So I said: Should I remember them? I said: By your messenger whom you sent. He said: By your prophet whom you sent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10145","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Fitr told us, he said: Sa’d bin Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “What do you say, O Bara’, when you go to bed?” He said: I said: God and His Messenger. I know, he said: “When you go to bed in a clean state, lean on your right hand, then say: O God, I have surrendered my face to You, and I have entrusted my affairs to You. And I have turned my back to You, out of fear and desire for You. There is no refuge or refuge from You except in You. I believe in Your Book which you have sent down, and in Your Prophet. “By the One whom You have sent.” So I said as he said, except that I said: “By Your Messenger whom You have sent.” He placed his hand on my chest and said: “By Your Prophet whom You have sent.” Then he said: “Whoever says it the night before and then dies, dies on the Fitrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10146","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Sheikh Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you goes to bed at night, let him lean on his right hand, then To say: In the name of God, O God, I have surrendered myself to You, turned my back to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and turned my face to You. Out of fear of You and longing for You, there is no refuge or refuge except in You. I believed in Your revealed Book, and in your sent Prophet, who said it and then died. \He died on the verge of breaking the fast.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10147","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalaf, who is Ibn Khalifa, told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad, who is Ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go to bed, he would lean on his right hand, then he would say: “In the name of God, O God, I submit to Islam.” My soul is to You, I turn my back to You, I entrust my command to You, I turn my face to You, desiring You, and fearing You, and there is no refuge. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. So if he dies that night, he dies on the fitrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10148","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Muhajir Abi al-Hasan, he said: I heard Al-Baraa, And He did not raise it, for He commanded a man when he took his bed, to say: “O God, I have surrendered myself to You, and I have turned my face to You. And I entrusted my affairs to you, and I turned my back to you, out of desire and fear for you. There is no refuge or refuge from you except in you. I believed in your book which You sent down, and with Your Messenger whom You sent, so if he dies, he dies on the Fitrah.” Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, he said: Shu’bah told me, he said: Abu Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin A single person like that on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10149","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he went to bed every night, he would bring his hands together, then blow on them and recite between them: Say, He is Allah, One, and Say, I seek refuge. In the Lord of separation and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind. Then he wiped with them as much of his body as he could, starting with them on his head and face and the front. his body, he does this three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10150","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was One of the last things he would say when he slept while placing his hand on his right cheek and seeing that he had died that night was: “Lord of the heavens.” The Seven Lord of the Great Throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, the One who sent down the Torah and the Gospel and the Criterion, the Creator of love and intentions, I seek refuge in You from everything. You are taking his command, O God, You are the First and there is nothing before You, and You are the Last and there is nothing after You, and You are the Manifest and there is nothing above You. And You are the Inward One, and there is nothing besides You. Pay off my debt and enrich me from poverty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10151","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, he said: Abu Salih used to order us, if one of us wanted to sleep, to He lies on his right side, then says: “O God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of the Great Throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, so create love.” And the intentions, and the sender of the Torah and the Gospel and the Criterion, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose corner you take hold of. You are the first, and there is nothing before you. And you are the Last, and there is nothing after you. You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above you. You are the Hidden, so there is nothing below you. Pay off my debt, and make me rich from Poverty,” and he used to narrate that on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10152","Muhammad bin Maadan told us, he said: Ibn Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Sa’id bin told me Abu Sa`id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you goes to bed, let him shake off his bed inside his garment, for he does not know what he left behind it, then to lie down on his right side, then say: In your name, my Lord, I have placed By my side, and to You I raise it up. If You hold my soul, have mercy on it, and if You release it, protect it from the means with which You protect Your righteous servants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10153","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id Al-Maqbari told me. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When one of you goes to bed, let him remove the inside of his garment. Let him dust his bed with it, then lean on his right hand, and say: In your name, my Lord, I have placed my side, and in your name I raise it. Oh God, if you hold it So have mercy on her, and if you send her, protect her in the same way you protect your righteous servants.” Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamar bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: something similar. Ibn Mubarak stopped him. Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. . . . . . . . His saying (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10154","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim told us, he said: Hajjaj, who is the son of Muhammad, told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, he said: Ya’la told me Ibn Ata’, he said: I heard Amr Ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Tell me something that I should say in the morning and in the evening. He said: “Say: O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness. There is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and from the evil of Satan and his polytheism. Say it in the morning and in the evening, and when you take \your bed\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10155","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he commanded a man when he went to bed to say: “O God, you created my soul, and you “Give her death, her death and her life are yours. If you keep her alive, protect her, and if she causes her to die, forgive her. Oh God, I ask you for well-being.” A man said to him: Did you hear this from Omar? He said: Who is better than Omar: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10156","Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: It was When Ibn Umar went to bed, he said: “O God, you created my soul, and you take its life. Its death and its life are yours. O God, if If you cause her to die, forgive her, and if you bring her back to life, protect her. Oh God, I ask you for well-being.” Then a man from his descendants said to him: Oh my father, Was Omar saying this? He said: Rather, it is better than Omar who used to say this."
"10157","Amr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, he said: My father told us, he said: Hussein told us, he said: Ibn Buraidah, he said: Ibn Omar told me that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would say: “Praise be to God who is sufficient for me and sustains me.” And he fed me, and gave me drink, and he who bestowed upon me the best, and the one who gave me the most bountiful, praise be to God in every condition, O God, the Lord of all things and the King of all Everything, and everything is Yours, I seek refuge in You from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10158","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would say: “Praise be to God who has fed us, given us drink, sufficed us, and sheltered us. How many “There is no one to suffice or shelter him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10159","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa, on the authority of Jabalah He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: Teach me something that will benefit me. He said: “When you go to bed, say: O disbelievers until you seal it, for it is a release from polytheism.”"
"10160","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then what brought you back?” He said: I said: I have come, O Messenger of God, to teach me. Something I say when I sleep. He said: “When you go to bed, recite: Say, O you disbelievers, then sleep at the end of it, for it is \free from polytheism\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10161","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, On the authority of his father, he said: Zayd bin Thabit came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him to teach him something to say when he went to bed. He said: “Recite: Say, O you disbelievers, then sleep at the end of it, for it is a disavowal of polytheism.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10162","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Farwa al-Ashja’i, On the authority of a companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever recites Say, O you disbelievers, when he dreams He has been freed from polytheism.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10163","Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa Al-Ashja’i said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “Read: Say, ‘O you disbelievers,’ when you dream, for it is an acquittal from \polytheism\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10164","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, and Asim, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Dhabiya. On the authority of Muadh, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever goes to bed in a pure state, remembers God Almighty until his eyes overcome him, and he is disgraced by “At night, he did not ask God Almighty for any good of the good of this world and the hereafter but He gave it to him.” Thabit said: Then Abu Dhabiyya came to us and told us about this. Hadith, on the authority of Muadh (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10165","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: It was me, Asim and Thabit, so Asim told, on the authority of A month ago, on the authority of Abu Dhabiyah, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Muslim spends the night watching a pure penis.” Then he would feel exhausted at night, asking God for good in this world and the hereafter, but I would give him.” Thabit said: Then he came to us and told us this hadith, and no I know him, but he meant Abu Dhabiyah, so I said to Hammad: On the authority of Muadh? He said: On the authority of Muadh"
"10166","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiya, on the authority of Shahr Ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Umamah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well will go Sin is from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.” Abu Dhabiya Al-Homsi said: I heard Amr bin Absa narrating this hadith, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: And I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever spends the night pure in remembrance of God will not be disturbed for an hour of the night, asking “Allah has nothing in it regarding the matter of this world or the hereafter unless He gives it to him.” Shimr bin Atiya disagreed with them"
"10167","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Alaa bin Usaym told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, the uncle of Shimr bin Atiya, on the authority of A month, he said: Abu Dhabiyya told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Absa, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No man “A Muslim spends the night in a state of purity, remembering God, then he gets naked at night and asks God for the good of this world and the hereafter, unless He gives it to him.” Muhammad bin Hisham told us, he said: Al-Fadl, meaning Ibn Al-Ala, told us, he said: Fitr informed us, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiya, on the authority of a month, He said: Abu Dhabiyya told us, I heard Amr bin Absa, something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10168","Muhammad bin Bashar told me, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah says. And Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Babah On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Whoever says in his sleep: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is over all Everything is powerful, and there is no power nor strength except in God. Glory be to God and praise be to Him. There is no god but God. God is great. His sins are forgiven, even if “It was more than the foam of the sea.” Not in the hadith of Shu’bah: in his dream, it was said by Abu Abd al-Rahman. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10169","Ahmad bin Abdul Wahhab told me, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Musa told us, he said: Hilal, meaning Ibn Haqq, told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, On the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of two men from Banu Hanzalah, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No servant A Muslim goes to his bed and recites a surah from the Book of God when he goes to bed, except that God has appointed over him an angel who will not let anything come near him or harm him. Until it blows whenever it blows.”"
"10170","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Sulayman bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Much good is one whom few know. After every obligatory prayer, there are ten tasbihat al-tasbihat, ten takbeers, and ten praises. That is one hundred. Fifty on the tongue, and one thousand and five hundred on the scale, and when he places it on his side, he glorifies God thirty-three times, and praises God thirty-three times, And God says “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times, so that is a hundred on the tongue, and a thousand and five hundred on the scale, so which of you works day and night? \Two thousand and five hundred is bad?\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10171","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali: that Fatima The daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to use him as a servant. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not tell you something?” Is it better for you than it? She said: What is it? He said: “You glorify God thirty-three times in your sleep, say Akbar thirty-three, and give thanks thirty-four.” Sufyan said: I don’t know which are four. Thirty. Ali said: I have not abandoned it since I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was said: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even on the night of Siffin (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10172","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Al-Awam told us, he said: Amr bin Murrah told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and put his foot between me and Fatima, so we learned what When we go to bed, we say: “Thirty-three tasbihs, thirty-three praises, and thirty-four takbirs.” Ali said: What I left it after that, and a man said to him: Not even on the night of Siffin? He said: Not even on the night of Siffin"
"10173","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Amr ibn Malik and Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka`b, on the authority of Shabath ibn Rabi’i, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: He came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A captive was delivered, and Ali said to Fatima: Go to your father and ask him for a servant who can be pious about work. So she came to her father in the evening, and he said to her: “What’s the matter with you?” “Daughter?” She said: “Nothing. I came to greet you, and you were ashamed to ask anything, until the midwife was there.” He said: “Come to your father and ask him.” A servant who feared her work, so she went out until she came to him. He said: “What is the matter with you, daughter?” She said: Nothing, father. I came to see how evening, and she was ashamed to ask him anything, until, when it was the third night, Ali said to her: Go, so they all went out, until they came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What brings you here?” Then Ali said to him: Meaning the Messenger of God, the work is difficult for us, so we wanted you to give it to us. As a servant to protect us from work, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I direct you to something better for you than red camels?” Then Ali said: Yes, O The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon you, said: “A hundred times of greatness, glorifications, and praises. When you two want to sleep, then spend the night praying a thousand good deeds. And the same is true when the morning comes.” Ali said: “I have not missed it since I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except on the night of Siffin. I forgot about her until I remembered her at the end of the night (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10174","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abu Musab told us, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Dinar narrated to him, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, On the authority of Al-Maqbari Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, the client of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “And no one goes to his bed and does not mention God therein unless there is a burden upon him.” Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10175","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever lies down and does not remember God therein, there will be a reproach from God for him.” Brief"
"10176","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Two are easy, and whoever does them is a little, and whoever maintains them will enter Paradise.” We said: O Messenger of God. God, what are they? He said: “When one of you has finished his prayer, he says “Tasbih-Tasbih” ten times, and “Thanksgiving” ten times, and “Allahu Akbar” ten times, and if he wants to sleep for a hundred days, that is. Two hundred and fifty with the tongue, and two thousand and five hundred with the balance. Which of you does two thousand and five hundred in his day and night? “Bad.” Abdullah said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tying it with his hand. The common people stopped (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10177","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr said: “Whoever says at the end of every obligatory prayer ten praises, ten glorifications, and ten takbeers, and if he wants to He recites thirty-three times of tasbih, thirty-three times of praise, and thirty-four times of takbeer, and if he continues to recite them, he will enter Paradise.”"
"10178","Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Ash’ath told us, he said: Abu Mushar told us, he said: Haql bin Ziyad told us, he said: he told me Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God One hundred times before sunrise and before sunset is better than one hundred camels, and whoever says: Praise be to God a hundred times before sunrise And before its sunset, it is better than a hundred horses mounted on it, and whoever says: God is greater a hundred times before the sun rises and before it sets. It is better than freeing a hundred slaves, and whoever says: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is over everything. Almighty one hundred times before the sun rises and before it sets. No one will come on the Day of Resurrection with a deed better than his except the one who said what he said. \or more\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10179","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, he said: Abu Balaj claimed that Amr bin Maymun told them that he heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whatever is on the earth A man says: There is no god but God, and God is great, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, except that his sins are forgiven, even if they were more than \sea foam\"""""
"10180","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: “Because I say: Glory be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is the greatest, and praise be to God, that is more beloved to me than being burdened with Her number of horses, with their armor, in the cause of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10181","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Al-Jariri. On the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What do we say in our prostration? He said: “What God has chosen for His angels: Glory be to God and praise be to Him.” It was narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10182","Malik bin Saad told us, he said: Spirit told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Jariri, he said: I heard Sawada bin Asim Al-Anazi narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever loves speaking to God Glory be to Him, may He be glorified and exalted, for the servant to say: Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10183","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, God will remove from him his sins, even if It was more than the foam of the sea.”"
"10184","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God the Great, a tree will be planted for him in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10185","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ismail bin Bishr bin Mansour, and Muhammad bin Fayyad told us, they said: Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man while he was on a journey, saying: “God is great, God is great.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the Fitrah.” He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” He said: “He came out of the Fire,” so he preceded the people. If a shepherd was approaching prayer, he stood up and called the call to prayer. Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abd al-Ala bin Hammad told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10186","Muhammad bin Adam informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Fudayl. And Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Two words that are light on the tongue, heavy in the scale, and beloved to the Most Gracious: Glory be to God and praise be to Him. Glory be to God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10187","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told me, he said: Musa bin Ibrahim bin Kathir Al-Ansari Al-Madani told us, he said: I heard Talha bin Kharash, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The best remembrance is: There is no god but God.” “The best supplication is praise be to God.”"
"10188","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Saleh bin Saeed told me, recently, He submitted it to Suleiman bin Yasar, to a man from the Ansar: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Noah said to his son: I will recommend to you With a commandment, and keep it brief so that you do not forget it. I enjoin you with two, and I forbid you from two: As for the two I command you, God rejoices in them. And the righteousness of his creation, and they are often seeking God Almighty. I command you: There is no god but God. For if the heavens and the earth were a chain, it would break them apart. Even if it were on a scale and their weight, I advise you to say: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, for it is the prayer of creation, and by it creation is provided for, even if there are Nothing but glorifies His praise, but you do not understand their glorification. Indeed, He is Forbearing, Forgiving, and as for the two things He forbade, God hides from them. And his good character, he forbade you from polytheism and arrogance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10189","Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Yazid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “No servant says: There is no god but God sincerely, but the gates of heaven will be opened for him until they lead to the Throne, as long as they have been avoided.” \The major sins\"""""
"10190","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, in his hadith on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that a biker, Abu al-Samh He told him, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Moses said: O Lord, teach me something. I remind you of it and I call upon you by it. He said: O Moses: There is no god but God. Moses said: O Lord: all of your servants say this. He said: Say: There is no god but God. He said: There is no god but You. I just want something that you can specialize in for me. He said: O Moses, if only the seven heavens and their ruler were other than me, and the seven earths were on one hand. There is no god but God, on a scale that turned towards them, “There is no god but God.”"
"10191","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Because I say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and God is the greatest, and there is no god but God, more beloved to me than anything I have ever seen.” \the sun\"""""
"10192","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Harami bin Hafs told us, he said: Ubaid bin Mahran told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan talking, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is one of you unable to work every day like Uhud?” They said: O Messenger. God, and who can do it? He said: “All of you can do it.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what is it? He said: “Glory be to God, who is greater than anyone, and there is no god but God who is greater than anyone, and praise be to God, who is greater than anyone, and God is greater than anyone.”"
"10193","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, on the authority of Marwan, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, he said: My brother told me, that he heard his grandfather Abu Salam, He says: Abdullah bin Farroukh told me, he said: Aisha told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The son of Adam was created to Three hundred and sixty joints, so whoever exalts God, praises God, glorifies God, removes a stone from the path of Muslims, removes a thorn, or He isolated a bone, or enjoined what was right, or forbade what was wrong, the number of those three-sixty and three-hundred salamis that evening, and he had moved himself away. \from the fire\"""""
"10194","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Othman told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, Talha bin Ubaid Allah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no one better “In the sight of God, there is a believer who lives long in Islam, and who often glorifies Him, glorifies Him, glorifies Him, and praises Him.” Issa bin Yunus disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10195","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa, who is Ibn Ayan, told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Talha told us Ibn Yahya, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Muhammad Ibn Talha, who said: Shaddad Ibn Al-Hadi told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What “No one is greater in the sight of God than a believing man who lives in Islam.” He mentioned from His recitation and glorification. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10196","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Dirar bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “God has chosen four words: Glory be to God, praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is the Greatest. So whoever says: Glory be to God, twenty good deeds will be recorded for him, and twenty bad deeds will be removed from him. And whoever says: God is the Greatest, And like that, and whoever says: There is no god but Allah, then like that, and whoever says: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, on his own behalf, thirty good deeds, and thirty bad deeds are removed from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10197","Muhammad bin Ali bin Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best speeches are four, do not care which of them you begin with: Glory be to God, Praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10198","Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of some of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most beloved words to God are four. It does not matter to you whichever one you begin with: Glory be to God, and praise be to God.” To God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest.” Suhail bin Abi Saleh disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10199","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Saluli, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “God chose the words The most beloved speech to God is: There is no god but God, and God is the greatest, and glory be to God, and praise be to God. So whoever says: There is no god but God, then it is The word of sincerity, God records for him twenty good deeds and atones for him twenty bad deeds, and whoever says: God is great, that is the majesty of God. God records for him twenty good deeds and atones for him twenty bad deeds. And whoever says: Glory be to God, God records for him twenty good deeds and atones for him. He has twenty bad deeds on his behalf, and whoever says: Praise be to God, that is God’s praise, and His praise is praise, God will record for him thirty good deeds therein, and he will expiate. thirty bad deeds from him.”"
"10200","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Musa bin Khalaf told us, he said: Asim bin Bahdala told us, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me one day, and I said: Tell me something to do while I She was sitting, and he said: “Glorify God a hundred times, for it is equivalent to a hundred slaves from the descendants of Ishmael, and praise God a hundred times.” It is equivalent to one hundred saddled and bridled horses that you ride in the path of God. Say the takbir one hundred times, for it is equivalent to one hundred. “A full, imitated body, kissing it, and I will praise God a hundred times.” Abu Khalaf said: I do not think it is anything other than that he said: “It fills what is between the sky and the earth.”"
"10201","Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, he said: Abdul Samad told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Umaylah, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I love speaking to There are four things to God: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest. It does not matter which one you start with.” Jarir disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10202","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The most beloved words to God are four: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, God is great, and He will not harm you.” “Which one did you start with?” Salama bin Kuhayl disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10203","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If I narrate to you a hadith, do not add more than four good words that are from the Qur’an. It does not matter to you whichever one you begin with.” “Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10204","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Hafs bin Omar Al-Hawdi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muslim told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take your Paradise,” they said. : O Messenger of God, is there an enemy present? He said: “No, but your Paradise from the Fire will be the saying: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, for the Day of Resurrection will come.” On the Resurrection, they will be avoided and removed, and they are the righteous ones who will remain.”"
"10205","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most beloved of speech is God means that the servant says: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is your glory, and there is no god but You, and indeed I hate speech to God is such that a man says to another man, “Fear God,” and he says, “It is up to you.” Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, He said: Abdullah said: “One of the most beloved words to God is for a man to say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is Your glory. There is no god but You. My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins. No one forgives sins except You, and indeed it is the greatest sin in the sight of God.” Like him. Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Mus’ab told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, with this chain of transmission like it, and he said: On the authority of Abd God is “the one who loves words” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10206","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “One of the greatest sins in the sight of God is when a servant is told, ‘Fear God,’ and he says, ‘You have to blame yourself.’ And among the best of speech is for him to say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You. My Lord, I have done evil and wronged myself, so forgive me.”"
"10207","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad told us, he said: Shababah told us, he said: al-Mughirah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man enters his house, or goes to his bed, an angel and a devil come to him, and the angel says: Open Fine, and Satan says: Open with evil, so if he mentions God, the king will expel Satan and he continues to afflict him, so when he wakes up from his dream An angel and a devil approached him, and the king said: Open with good, and Satan said: Open with bad. If it is, he said: Praise be to God who responded. To myself after her death and he did not cause her to die in her sleep. Praise be to God who holds the seven heavens from falling on the earth except by His permission. At the end of the verse, if he falls from his bed and dies, he is a martyr, and if he stands up to pray, he will pray in virtues.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10208","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a man goes to bed, an angel and a devil come to him, and the angel says: End well. And Satan says: End with good news. If he mentions God and then sleeps, the angel spends the night eating him. When he wakes up, the angel says: Open with good. And Satan said: Open with evil, so if he said: Praise be to God who returned my soul to me and did not kill it in its sleep, praise be to God who keeps the heavens and the earth from falling on the earth except by His permission until the end of the verse. He fell from his bed and died and entered Paradise.” Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Azhar bin Al-Qasim told us, then he mentioned a word that means: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawaf, On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said, “If a man enters his house and goes to his bed,” then the hadith is invalidated, with a conditional (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10209","Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Rab’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up from his sleep, he would say: “Praise be to God who raised us after our death.” And to Him is the resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10210","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, he would say: “Praise be to God who brought us back to life after He caused us to die, and to Him “The resurrection” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10211","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Malik Ibn Umair, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Rabi’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, he would say: “Praise be to God.” To God is the One who gave us life after He had caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.”"
"10212","Muhammad bin Adam told me, on the authority of Sulayman, who is Ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, he said: “Praise be to God who brought us back to life after He caused us to die.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10213","Maymoon bin Abbas told us, he said: Saad bin Hafs Kufi told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Kharshah bin Al-Harr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to sleep, he would say: “In your name.” Oh God, let me die and live.” And when he woke up from his sleep, he said: “Praise be to God who brought us back to life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10214","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa ibn Bahloul informed us, saying: Al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to me, he said: Umair ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Junada bin Abi Umayyah narrated to me, he said: Ubadah bin Al-Samit narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever gets naked at night He said: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah. My Lord, forgive me, may He be forgiven. If he gets up and prays, his prayer will be accepted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10215","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Rabi’ah told me Ibn Ka'b said: I spent the night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing his ablution and his needs, and he used to get up during the night and say: Glory be to God and with His praise, Glory be to my Lord the Great and with His praise, Glory be to my Lord and with His praise.” Then he says: “Glory be to the Lord of the worlds, Glory be to Him.” Lord of the worlds\""
10216"""
"10216","Suwayd ibn Nasr informed us, saying: 'Abdullah informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), he said: ""A man from the people of Paradise will now appear before you."" Then a man from the Ansar appeared, his beard dripping with water from his ablution, holding his two sandals in his left hand. The next day, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A man from the people of Paradise will now appear before you."" That same man appeared in the same state as the first time. The third day, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A man from the people of Paradise will now appear before you."" That same man appeared in the same state as the first time. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As followed him. He said: ""I had a falling out with my father and swore not to enter his house for three nights. If you see fit to shelter me until my oath is resolved, then do so."" He said: ""Yes."" Anas said: So 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As narrated that he stayed with him for a night or three nights. He did not see him perform any voluntary night prayer, except that whenever he turned over on his bed, he would remember Allah and say Allahu Akbar until he got up for the Fajr prayer and performed a complete ablution. 'Abdullah said: Except that I never heard him say anything but good. When the three nights passed, I almost belittled his deeds. I said: ""O 'Abdullah, there was no anger or estrangement between me and my father, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say to you three times in three gatherings: 'A man from the people of Paradise will now appear before you,' and you appeared those three times. So I wanted to stay with you to observe your deeds, but I did not see you perform any great deed. So what is it that has brought you to the level the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned?"" He said: ""It is nothing but what you saw."" So I turned away from him. When I was leaving, he called me back and said: ""It is nothing but what you saw, except that I do not find in myself any deceit (ghish) toward any of the Muslims, nor do I envy anyone for any good that Allah has given him."" 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr said: ""This is what has brought you to that rank, and it is that which we cannot bear."""
"10217","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Yusuf bin Adi told us, he said: he told us Otham bin Ali, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was starved At night, he said: “There is no god but Allah, the One, the Supreme, Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the Mighty, the Forgiving.”"
"10218","Amr ibn Sawad informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Sa`id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, about. And Ubayd Allah bin Fadhalah told me, he said: Abdullah told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up at night, he would say: “No There is no god but You, Glory be to You. O God, I seek Your forgiveness for my sin, and I ask You for your mercy. O God, increase my knowledge and do not deviate my heart after You have guided me, and grant me mercy from Yourself, for You are the Giver.”"
"10219","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibn Abi Omar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Kitten, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he wakes up, let him say: Praise be to God who has healed me in my body and restored my soul to me. And He gave me permission to mention it.”"
"10220","Ali bin Muhammad told me, he said: Khalaf told us, meaning Ibn Tamim, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: “God laughs at two men: a man who met the enemy while riding a horse of He represented the horses of his companions, but they were defeated and he stood still. If he was killed, he would be martyred, and if he survived, then he is the one at whom God laughs, and a man who rose in the depths of No one knew about the night, so he performed ablution and performed it well, then he thanked God and glorified Him, and sent blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and opened The Qur’an, for that is the one at whom God laughs. He says: “Look at my servant standing and no one sees him except me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10221","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he stood up to pray in the middle of the night, he would say: “O God, praise be to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You, You are the resurrection of the heavens.” And the earth, and praise be to You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and those in them. You are the truth, your word is the truth, your promise is the truth, and meeting you is the truth. And Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true. Oh God, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I return, and in You I disputed, and to you I judged, so forgive me what I have done before and what I have done in the future, and what I have expressed and what I have declared. You are my God, there is no god but You.”"
"10222","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He was asked Abdullah: What is the supplication with which you prayed for the night? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ask and it will be given to you.” He said: I said: “Oh God, I ask you “Faith that does not waver, and bliss that never ends, and accompanying our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the highest level of Paradise, the Paradise of eternity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10223","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Asbagh bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan. He said: Rabi’ah Al-Jarashi told me, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: The Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not recite when he got up to pray during the night. And what was he opening with? She said: He used to say “Allahu Akbar” ten times, praise “Allaah” ten times, say “Tasbih” ten times, say “Allah Allah” ten times, ask God for forgiveness ten times, and say: “O God, forgive me.” “Guide me, and provide for me” ten times, and he says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from distress on the Day of Judgment” ten times."
"10224","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told me, he said: Omar bin Jatham told me, he said: Al-Azhar bin Abdullah told me Al-Harazi, he said: Shariq Al-Hawzani told me, he said: I went to Aisha and asked her: What was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to open? Prayer when he wakes up at night? She said: Whenever he rose in the night, he would say “Allahu Akbar” ten times, and “Praise be to God” ten times, and he would say: “In the name of God and with His praise” ten times, and he would say: “Glory be to God.” The Holy King “ten times, asked forgiveness ten times, and glorified God ten times, and said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the distress of this world and the distress of the Day of Resurrection” ten times, then he begins the prayer"
"10225","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far, who is Ibn Sulaiman, told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Aisha. She said: I said: O Messenger of God, if I knew which night is the Night of Decree, what should I say about it? He said: “Say: O God, you are pardoning and love forgiveness, so forgive me.”"
"10226","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Kahms, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, She said: I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: If Laylat al-Qadr comes, what should I say? He said: “You say: O God, you are pardoning and love to pardon, so pardon me.” Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard a whisper, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, that Aisha said: Oh A prophet of God has been sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10227","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Marzouk, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: O Messenger of God Have you seen that if Laylat al-Qadr comes, what should I pray for? He said: “Say: O God, you are pardoning and love well-being, so pardon me.”"
"10228","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, if Laylat al-Qadr comes, what should I ask God during it? He said: “Say: O God, you are pardoning and love forgiveness, so forgive me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10229","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of Aisha, said: I said: O Messenger of God, have you considered that if Laylat al-Qadr came, what would Should I say that? He said: “Say: O God, you are pardoning and love forgiveness, so forgive me.”"
"10230","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jubayr, and he was a partner in a stolen property. Al-Silsilah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “If I knew which night is Laylat al-Qadr, my supplication would be to I ask God for forgiveness and well-being.”"
